<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>KMLMM: Import and export between KML and MiraMon format</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
   < <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
  <p>This application imports and exports between the KML format of GoogleEarth and MiraMon.</p>
 <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.--> 

  <p>The application creates a map with a point layer (PNT), which contains the
  'Point' type KML objects, a (ARC/NOD) line layer for KML objects of
  the 'LineString' type and a layer of polygons that contains the
  'Polygon' type objects, if there are any. 'MultiGeometry'
  and 'LinearRing' type objects that are not part of a polygon are
  ignored. If there is information regarding the z of each vertex, it is also
  converted. The layers are not structured topologically.</p>

  <p>The 'id' attribute and the 'name', 'description'
  y 'styleUrl' elements of each KML object are included. They are all
  added to the main table of each layer as thematic attributes under the
  names: ID_ENTITAT, NOM, DESCRIPCIO e ID_ESTIL.</p>

  <p>The map allows you to open all the layers created with symbolization,
  which for lines and polygons depends on the field values 'ID_ESTIL'
  and for the points is a radius point 3 with a text with the value of the
  'NOM' attribute of the object.</p>

  <p>All the objects of any KML file are in latitude/longitude projection with
  WGS84 datum, but the application allows you to reproject the map layers to any
  of the reference systems described in the MiraMon geodesic tables.</p>
  <hr/>

  <exclusiva>
